{"id": "spring-expression/src/main/java/org/springframework/expression/spel/ast/ValueRef.java::24::0", "file": "spring-expression/src/main/java/org/springframework/expression/spel/ast/ValueRef.java", "module": "spring-expression", "block_start": 24, "start": 25, "end": 30, "indent": "", "lines": ["Represents a reference to a value.  With a reference it is possible to get or set the", "value. Passing around value references rather than the values themselves can avoid", "incorrect duplication of operand evaluation. For example in 'list[index++]++' without", "a value reference for 'list[index++]' it would be necessary to evaluate list[index++]", "twice (once to get the value, once to determine where the value goes) and that would", "double increment index."]}
