{"id": "spring-expression/src/main/java/org/springframework/expression/spel/standard/SpelCompiler.java::41::0", "file": "spring-expression/src/main/java/org/springframework/expression/spel/standard/SpelCompiler.java", "module": "spring-expression", "block_start": 41, "start": 42, "end": 44, "indent": "", "lines": ["A SpelCompiler will take a regular parsed expression and create (and load) a class", "containing byte code that does the same thing as that expression. The compiled form of", "an expression will evaluate far faster than the interpreted form."]}
{"id": "spring-expression/src/main/java/org/springframework/expression/spel/standard/SpelCompiler.java::41::1", "file": "spring-expression/src/main/java/org/springframework/expression/spel/standard/SpelCompiler.java", "module": "spring-expression", "block_start": 41, "start": 46, "end": 55, "indent": "", "lines": ["<p>The SpelCompiler is not currently handling all expression types but covers many of", "the common cases. The framework is extensible to cover more cases in the future. For", "absolute maximum speed there is *no checking* in the compiled code. The compiled", "version of the expression uses information learned during interpreted runs of the", "expression when it generates the byte code. For example if it knows that a particular", "property dereference always seems to return a Map then it will generate byte code that", "expects the result of the property dereference to be a Map. This ensures maximal", "performance but should the dereference result in something other than a map, the", "compiled expression will fail - like a ClassCastException would occur if passing data", "of an unexpected type in a regular Java program."]}
{"id": "spring-expression/src/main/java/org/springframework/expression/spel/standard/SpelCompiler.java::41::2", "file": "spring-expression/src/main/java/org/springframework/expression/spel/standard/SpelCompiler.java", "module": "spring-expression", "block_start": 41, "start": 57, "end": 61, "indent": "", "lines": ["<p>Due to the lack of checking there are likely some expressions that should never be", "compiled, for example if an expression is continuously dealing with different types of", "data. Due to these cases the compiler is something that must be selectively turned on", "for an associated SpelExpressionParser (through the {@link SpelParserConfiguration}", "object), it is not on by default."]}
{"id": "spring-expression/src/main/java/org/springframework/expression/spel/standard/SpelCompiler.java::41::3", "file": "spring-expression/src/main/java/org/springframework/expression/spel/standard/SpelCompiler.java", "module": "spring-expression", "block_start": 41, "start": 63, "end": 63, "indent": "", "lines": ["<p>Individual expressions can be compiled by calling {@code SpelCompiler.compile(expression)}."]}
{"id": "spring-expression/src/main/java/org/springframework/expression/spel/standard/SpelCompiler.java::92::0", "file": "spring-expression/src/main/java/org/springframework/expression/spel/standard/SpelCompiler.java", "module": "spring-expression", "block_start": 92, "start": 93, "end": 96, "indent": "\t", "lines": ["Attempt compilation of the supplied expression. A check is made to see", "if it is compilable before compilation proceeds. The check involves", "visiting all the nodes in the expression AST and ensuring enough state", "is known about them that bytecode can be generated for them."]}
{"id": "spring-expression/src/main/java/org/springframework/expression/spel/standard/SpelCompiler.java::129::0", "file": "spring-expression/src/main/java/org/springframework/expression/spel/standard/SpelCompiler.java", "module": "spring-expression", "block_start": 129, "start": 130, "end": 131, "indent": "\t", "lines": ["Generate the class that encapsulates the compiled expression and define it.", "The generated class will be a subtype of CompiledExpression."]}
{"id": "spring-expression/src/main/java/org/springframework/expression/spel/standard/SpelCompiler.java::192::0", "file": "spring-expression/src/main/java/org/springframework/expression/spel/standard/SpelCompiler.java", "module": "spring-expression", "block_start": 192, "start": 193, "end": 196, "indent": "\t", "lines": ["Load a compiled expression class. Makes sure the classloaders aren't used too much", "because they anchor compiled classes in memory and prevent GC. If you have expressions", "continually recompiling over time then by replacing the classloader periodically", "at least some of the older variants can be garbage collected."]}
{"id": "spring-expression/src/main/java/org/springframework/expression/spel/standard/SpelCompiler.java::222::0", "file": "spring-expression/src/main/java/org/springframework/expression/spel/standard/SpelCompiler.java", "module": "spring-expression", "block_start": 222, "start": 223, "end": 225, "indent": "\t", "lines": ["Factory method for compiler instances. The returned SpelCompiler will", "attach a class loader as the child of the given class loader and this", "child will be used to load compiled expressions."]}
{"id": "spring-expression/src/main/java/org/springframework/expression/spel/standard/SpelCompiler.java::246::0", "file": "spring-expression/src/main/java/org/springframework/expression/spel/standard/SpelCompiler.java", "module": "spring-expression", "block_start": 246, "start": 247, "end": 249, "indent": "\t", "lines": ["Request that an attempt is made to compile the specified expression.", "It may fail if components of the expression are not suitable for compilation", "or the data types involved are not suitable for compilation. Used for testing."]}
{"id": "spring-expression/src/main/java/org/springframework/expression/spel/standard/SpelCompiler.java::258::0", "file": "spring-expression/src/main/java/org/springframework/expression/spel/standard/SpelCompiler.java", "module": "spring-expression", "block_start": 258, "start": 259, "end": 260, "indent": "\t", "lines": ["Request to revert to the interpreter for expression evaluation.", "Any compiled form is discarded but can be recreated by later recompiling again."]}
